<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · other</p><h1 class="enc-title">Regeneration (Switzerland)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1830–1848</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Regeneration was the period of Swiss history from 1830 to 1848 in which liberal movements, encouraged by the July Revolution in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, won new constitutions in most cantons, introducing popular <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a>, freedom of the press and equality before the law. Conflict between liberal and conservative cantons, sharpened by religion, culminated in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sonderbund-war">Sonderbund War</a> and the federal state of 1848.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/regeneration-switzerland.jpg" alt="Regeneration (Switzerland)" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Own work · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Switzerland_2-3.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
